            "text": " between rounds 8 and 9, 2.5 cm apart. Stuff the head and body firmly. Leave the tail lightly stuffed so it curves naturally. Sew the head to the top of the body. Attach arms to either side of the body at round 4 from the top. Pin the tail in a curve at the back before sewing down; catch it at the base and at the midpoint with tacking stitches."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
